\chu{\sfi Ferrihydrite slurry:}
\chu{Slowly titrate 400 ml of 20 mM FeCl$_3$$\cdot$6H$_2$O solution with 10% (w/v) NaOH to pH 7.0-7.5 with agitation on a magnetic stirrer.  Wash the precipitate with distilled water three times.  Remove the ferrihydrite suspension into a container, cover with water and store at room temperature overnight.   Remove supernatant after centrifugation at 2000 rpm for 5 min.  Distribute ferrihydrite slurry to culture vessels before pouring the medium described above (final frrihydrite concentration is approximately 50 mM in medium).}

