N$_2$--CO$_2$ (4:1, v/v) gas stream.  Distribute the medium into culture vessels
(e.g., 9 ml of the medium in Hungate tubes) under a N$_2$--CO$_2$ (4:1, v/v) gas
mixture, seal with butyl rubber stoppers and autoclave.  Separately
autoclave 0.2 M sodium lactate under a N$_2$ atmosphere.  After cooling, add
1/9 volume of the sodium lactate solution, and filter--sterilized 8\% NaHCO$_3$
solution, Vitamin solution, Thiamine solution and Vitamin B$_1$$_2$ solution to
the medium.  Readjust pH to 7.0, if necessary.  Prior to use, reduce the
medium with Na$_2$S$\cdot$9H$_2$O (3\% solution, autoclaved and stocked under N$_2$).}

